{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"creased-dermal-hogget","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nDiscovered during ticket c465 (PydanticAIRunner lifecycle revalidation, epic\nfinancial-stoneware-brant). In `PydanticAIRunner.run()` (src/rebar/llm/runner.py), the\nfinalization/spend-recording tail runs strictly AFTER both:\n- the `with ProviderSession(...) as provider_session:` block has exited (runner.py:452-708),\n  and\n- the failure-accounting `try/except/finally` around the agent call (runner.py:605-707).\n\nConcretely: `log_call_success` (:716) fires, THEN `_findings.finalize_outcome` (:725) runs,\nTHEN `record_call_spend` (:751). If `finalize_outcome` raises (e.g. schema validation failure\non a structured/verify_completion call), the exception propagates raw out of `run()`:\n- `log_call_success` already fired (by design — its docstring explicitly wants this).\n- `record_call_spend` NEVER fires — the call already burned real tokens but leaves no spend\n  row in usage.jsonl / the billable-CI sink.\n- `interpret_failure`/`usage_log.record_failure`/`step_failures.record` are also skipped,\n  since they live inside the already-closed except block around the agent call, not around\n  finalize_outcome.\n\nThis is the mirror case to bug 8455 (a raise DURING the agent call itself, which\n`usage_log.record_failure` in the except block now covers) — but 8455's fix does not reach\nthis later boundary.\n\nA characterization test pinning this CURRENT behavior was added in c465's landed change:\n`tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py::test_a_raise_in_finalize_outcome_still_logs_but_skips_the_spend_row`.\n\n## Problem\n\nA structured/verify_completion call that succeeds at the model level but fails schema\nvalidation in `finalize_outcome` silently loses its spend attribution — undercounting real\ntoken spend in cost reporting with no error surfaced for the loss itself (the ValueError/\nschema error IS raised to the caller, but nothing signals the missing spend row specifically).\n\n## Approach (not yet designed — this ticket is to decide and implement a fix)\n\nOptions to weigh: (a) wrap `finalize_outcome` so a spend row is recorded before propagating its\nraise (mirrors bug 8455's discipline for the agent-call except block); (b) move\n`record_call_spend` earlier, before `finalize_outcome`, if usage/token counts are already known\nat that point (they are — `usage` is populated before `log_call_success`); (c) some other\nnarrow fix. Whatever is chosen must not duplicate ProviderSession/ExitStack, must not introduce\na generic hook/plugin bus, and must be proven with a RED-before-GREEN test derived from the\ncharacterization test above (which pins CURRENT behavior and must be updated to pin the FIXED\nbehavior once this bug is resolved).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A raise in `finalize_outcome` still results in a spend row being recorded for tokens\n      already consumed by the call.\n- [ ] `test_a_raise_in_finalize_outcome_still_logs_but_skips_the_spend_row` (or its replacement)\n      is updated to assert the FIXED behavior (spend row present) rather than the gap.\n- [ ] No regression to the existing failure-accounting path for a raise during the agent call\n      itself (bug 8455's coverage).","id":"fe75-a4a3-9eef-457c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"record_call_spend is skipped when finalize_outcome raises (silent spend-row loss)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788054461804704001,"uuid":"f7dc8e09-ec0a-49af-8287-14b452609749"}